course: dictionary
lesson: 10562
title: Unclean: one word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have an everyday meaning and an older meaning from old laws or religious writing. «Unclean» is one of them. In «unclean water» it means dirty, which is the meaning you will meet most often.
explain: Read the words around it: «Vultures are scavengers whose very strong stomach acid kills most germs from rotting meat; when vultures nearly died out... carcasses lay uncleaned and disease spread.» The clue is disease spread, so unclean places are dirty places where germs can travel. Try your meaning in the sentence: dirty fits, so you are on the right track.
explain: In an old religious story, unclean means not pure, so a person had to be kept apart or washed before worship. The context tells you which meaning the writer means. Ask yourself: is this about dirt, or about rules and purity?
fact: Unclean means dirty or not clean, like unclean water or unclean hands.
fact: In old religious laws, «unclean» meant not pure, so a person or thing had to be kept apart or washed in a special way before worship.
fact: In old or religious writing, «unclean» can also mean morally bad or wicked.
fact: «Uncleaned» means not cleaned, as in «carcasses lay uncleaned».
fact: Unclean is an adjective: unclean, more unclean, most unclean.
exercise: Mum says the pool water looks unclean. What does unclean mean? | Warm and bubbly | *Dirty and not clean | Full of fish | Very quiet
exercise: In old religious laws, what did unclean mean? | Painted gold for a festival | Holy and blessed by a priest | *Not pure, so a person had to be kept apart or washed before worship | Very loud and noisy
exercise: In old or religious writing, unclean can also mean: | Sleepy and slow | *Morally bad or wicked | Covered in snow | Very tall
test: «Vultures... carcasses lay uncleaned and disease spread.» What does uncleaned suggest? | *Left dirty, so disease could spread | Carefully washed and polished | Eaten up quickly by children | Hidden under the sand
test: Which phrase describes hands that have not been washed? | Painted bright red | Very cold fingers | Holding a pen | *Unclean hands
exam: A pupil says «unclean» only appears in old Bible stories. Is this right? | No, it means very tall | Yes, it is never used in everyday life | Yes, but only in songs | *No, it also means dirty in everyday speech, like unclean water
